ple and Culture Health & Safety Wellness Finance and Planning IT Services Marketing & Communications Privacy at Algoma U Physical Plant Services Policies and Procedures Public Disclosure Documents Faculty Resources Jump To Student Portal Employee Portal Course Schedules Sault Ste. Marie Campus Brampton Campus Timmins Campus Wishart Library Bookstore & Supplies Thunderbirds Athletics Algoma U Shop Facebook Instagram Twitter YouTube LinkedIn Generic selectors Exact matches only Search in title Search in content Post Type Selectors Search Home > Academics > Career and Experiential Education > Career Hub > Work On Campus Work on Campus Algoma University is pleased to offer programs that enable students to work full-time during the summer, and part-time throughout the academic year while completing their studies. There are positions available for all students to apply to as well as positions available for eligible domestic students with a financial need. Regular Fall/Winter Part-Time Jobs Regular positions available for all students are posted on the Student Portal within the Resources section. Part-Time positions are available on or near campus in a variety of areas and are available to all Algoma University students. Jobs Posted: February 23, 2025 Closing Date: April 30, 2025 Work Study Program The Work Study Program (WSP) provides part-time employment opportunities on or near campus to eligible Algoma University students. This program is administered and overseen by the Financial Aid Office and is designed to assist eligible students with an unmet financial need. An application is required and can be submitted through the Algoma University Student Self-Service Portal within the Financial Aid section. Jobs start in September and go through until April. Fall/Winter 2026-27 Work Study Program (WSP) Applications Open: March 2, 2026 Applications Close: March 31, 2026 Summer Employment Program The Summer Employment Program (SEP) provides full-time employment opportunities on or near campus to eligible Algoma University students. This program is administered and overseen by the Financial Aid Office and is designed to assist returning eligible domestic students with an unmet financial need for their upcoming academic year. An application is required and can be submitted through the Self-Service Portal within the Financial Aid section. Jobs start in May and end in August. 2026 Summer Employment Program (SEP) Applications Open: January 5, 2026 Applications Close: January 31, 2026 Students that are approved to work through the Summer Employment Program will be invited to submit their resume for their preferred job position from February 3rd to February 13th. Departments are required to complete hiring by March 20th. For more information regarding the Work Study Program or Summer Employment Program, contact the Financial Aid Office (fao@algomau.ca) . Information for International Students on Work on Campus If you are an international student and you want to work on campus, there are certain regulations you’ll need to follow. Take a look at your options below. International Students Working Off-Campus If you are an international student studying in Canada, you must meet the following criteria to be eligible for a work permit under the Off –Campus Work Permit (OCWP).  Requirements are subject to change. Please visit www.cic.gc.ca for up-to-date information: You must have a valid study permit; You must have studied full-time at Algoma University for at least six months of the last 12 months before you apply; You must maintain satisfactory academic standing (as defined by Algoma University); and You must be enrolled in an academic program of study (not including SPELL). Students who hold a valid OCWP are permitted to work off-campus for a maximum of 20 hours a week during study periods and 40 hours a week during non-study periods. Interested in working after graduation? Students who have attended and graduated from academic programs with a two-year duration or longer are eligible for a post-graduate work permit for up to three years.  For more detailed information on this work permit, please contact the International Student Advisor. International Co-op Opportunities International students may choose to participate in our Co-operative Education Program (more commonly known as Co-op).  The Co-op Program is a certificate program that allows students to work in paid full-time positions that are relevant to their field of study.  Co-op requirements are as follows: Successfully complete COOP 0101 (career skills course); Complete 30 credits at Algoma University; Maintain a 70% or higher average (includes all course attempts); Register as a full-time student in two of the past four terms; and Apply for a Co-op Work Permit. Contact For more information please contact: Mark Allard International Student Advisor international@algomau.ca 705-949-2301, ext.4238 Office: SH 204 Career Planning We assist students with a wide variety of career planning needs. The tools provided are vital to gaining meaningful employment. Learn More Career Assistance Let’s get you ready for a job application! We assist students in all aspects that come with applying for a new job. Learn More Information for Employers Want to become ALL IN with Algoma university? Find out more about students and all that we have to offer. Learn More Facebook Instagram Twitter YouTube LinkedIn Special Mission Campus Safety Calendar Latest News Giving Careers Privacy Accessibility 1520 Queen Street East Sault Ste. Marie, Ontario Canada P6A 2G4 24 Queen St. East (A-101 Welcome Centre) Brampton, Ontario Canada L6V 1A3 Tel: 1-888-Algoma-U (1-888-254-6628) Info@algomau.ca Copyright © 2026 Algoma University. All Rights Reserved. Future. Focused. Sign up to learn more about what sets Algoma apart and to get application advice sent right to your inbox. All fields opposite are required to submit your interest. [gravityform id=\"11\" title=\"false\" description=\"false\" ajax=\"true\"] This website uses cookies to enhance your user experience, analyze site traffic, and support our digital services. By continuing to use this site, you agree to our use of cookies as outlined in our Notice of Website Privacy, Terms and Conditions . You can manage your cookie settings at any time. Select ‘Accept’ to continue, or see the Opt-Out section in the Notice of Website Privacy for details. Accept Close GDPR Cookie Settings Privacy Overview Strictly Necessary Cookies Powered by GDPR Cookie Compliance Privacy Overview This website uses cookies so that we can provide you with the best user experience possible. Cookie information is stored in your browser and performs functions such as recognising you when you return to our website and helping our team to understand which sections of the website you find most interesting and useful. Strictly Necessary Cookies Strictly Necessary Cookie should be enabled at all times so that we can save your preferences for cookie settings. Enable or Disable Cookies Enabled Disabled Enable All Save Settings"
